est approach: use the 3x3 fully populated block (9 cells) → 4 corners remain. This is a well-known Game of Life pattern.\n\nGen 0 = (0,0),(1,0),(2,0),(0,1),(1,1),(2,1),(0,2),(1,2),(2,2)\nGen 1 = (0,0),(2,0),(0,2),(2,2)\n\nLet me write this test:","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"## Red -- Test 10: 3x3 fully populated block (Rule 3 Overpopulation example)\n\nThe spec's example has internal inconsistencies, so I'll use the canonical 3x3 block which cleanly demonstrates overpopulation:\n- Gen 0: all 9 cells alive\n- Gen 1: only 4 corners remain (edges have 5 neighbors → die, center has 8 → dies)"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_52e19374553d412eb5b8fc82","name":"edit","arguments":{"edits":[{"newText":"  it(\"3x3 fully populated block: corners survive, others die (Rule 3 Overpopulation example)\", () => {\n    // 3x3 block: 4 corners have 3 neighbors -> survive; 4 edges have 5 -> die;\n    // center has 8 -> dies. Result: 4 corners remain.\n    expect(\n      sortCells(\n        nextGeneration([\n          [0, 0],\n          [1, 0],\n          [2, 0],\n          [0, 1],\n          [1, 1],\n          [2, 1],\n          [0, 2],\n          [1, 2],\n          [2, 2],\n        ])\n      )\n    ).toEqual([\n      [0, 0],\n      [0, 2],\n      [2, 0],\n      [2, 2],\n    ]);\n  });","oldText":"  it.todo(\"3x3 fully populated block: corners survive, others die (Rule 3 Overpopulation example)\");"}],"path":"/home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-25_09-28-53_game-of-life-example-mapping_v6.2.1-phase-continuation-pi_minimax-m3/src/game-of-life.spec.ts"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"tensorx/minimax-m3","usage":{"input":197,"output":3541,"cacheRead":71936,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":3136,"totalTokens":75674,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784975999449,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-ad5c5427-2491-4fd9-9d3d-c7daf2551302","responseModel":"minimax/minimax-m