...L_TROMINO]` - spread\n- Entry 3 output: `[...L_TROMINO, [1, 1]]` - 1 literal cell\n- Entry 4 input: 6 cells\n- Entry 4 output: 6 cells\n- Entry 5 input: spread\n- Entry 5 output: spread\n- Entry 6 input: `[...DIAMOND, [1, 1]]` - 1 literal cell\n- Entry 6 output: spread\n- Entry 7 input: 9 cells\n- Entry 7 output: 4 cells\n- Entry 8 input: 4 cells\n- Entry 8 output: 4 cells\n\nL_TROMINO definition: 3 cells\nDIAMOND definition: 4 cells\n\nTotal literal cells: 3 + 4 + (3+1) + (4+0) + (0+1) + (6+6) + (0+0) + (1+0) + (9+4) + (4+4) = 7 + 4 + 12 + 1 + 12 + 1 + 13 + 8 = 58\n\nActually I'm overcomplicating this. Let me use a simpler heuristic - count each literal coordinate pair as one constant.\n\nLooking at the implementation:\n- L_TROMINO: 3 constants\n- DIAMOND: 4 constants\n- Entry 1: 4 constants (3 input + 1 output)\n- Entry 2: 4 constants in input, 0 in output (uses L_TROMINO)\n- Entry 3: 0 in input, 1 in output (the new cell)\n- Entry 4: 12 constants\n- Entry 5: 0 in input, 0 in output (all uses DIAMOND)\n- Entry 6: 1 in input, 0 in output\n- Entry 7: 13 constants\n- Entry 8: 8 constants\n\nTotal: 3 + 4 + 4 + 4 + 1 + 12 + 1 + 13 + 8 = 50\n\n**Bindings** (Mass: 1):\n- `Cell` type alias (not really a binding, but a type)\n- `Pattern` type alias (not really a binding)\n- `L_TROMINO`, `DIAMOND`, `PATTERNS` constants: 3\n- `nextGeneration` parameter `cells`: 1\n- `cellKey` parameter: 2 (x, y)\n- `liveCells`: 1\n- `matches` parameter `expected`: 1\n- `x`, `y` destructuring: 2\n- Loop `for (const { input, output } of PATTERNS)`: 2\n\nTotal: 3 + 1 + 2 + 1 + 1 + 2 + 2 = 12\n\n**Invocations** (Mass: 2):\n- `cells.map(...)`: 1\n- `cellKey(x, y)` inside map: 1\n- `new Set(...)`: 1\n- `expected.length`: 1\n- `liveCells.size`: 1\n- `expected.every(...)`: 1\n- `liveCells.has(...)`: 1\n- `cellKey(x, y)` inside every: 1\n- `for...of` loop iteration: 1\n- `matches(input)`: 1\n- `[...output]`: 1 (spread, technically an invocation? maybe not)\n\nLet me be more careful:\n- `cells.map`